Rule 3 (input tensor is empty or only contains non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (reduction over valid dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (tensor shape matches input dimension size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 7 (tensor must be compatible with input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
